{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>כטומאת</b> bet. כטומאת נדתה כטומאת הנדה היתה וגו' — as is found in the Midrash, that He compares them to the impurity of a menstruating woman: just as a menstruating woman has purification through water, so too Israel has purification, as it is stated: וזרקתי עליכם מים וגו'. Alternatively, just as with a menstruating woman a priest may enter with her into a house, so too Israel — even though they are impure, the Divine Presence is among them, as it is stated: השוכן אתם בתוך טומאותם — and not like a corpse, with which a priest may not enter into a house. Eleven times in this pericah are written זבה זובו זובה, corresponding to the eleven days between menstruation and menstruation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:32.407567695Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}